    "methods_description": "Participants wore a 120-channel scalp EEG cap with 110 mechanically coupled noise electrodes and 8 neck EMG electrodes, recorded with 8 BrainVision amplifiers. They also wore Loadsol insoles and an APDM Opal IMU on the lower back, plus a safety harness and LCD goggles. Each 3-minute condition (0.0, 0.4, 0.8, 1.2, 1.6 m/s, in randomized order) included visual occlusions lasting 1.5 s every 8-10 s. A static scene was projected onto a screen in front of the treadmill.",
